<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shaan-Gan-Ning Border Region</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1937–1950</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Shaan-Gan-Ning Border Region was the Chinese Communist base area in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaanxi">Shaanxi</a> and parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu">Gansu</a> and Ningxia, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yanan">Yan'an</a>, from 1937 to 1950. Formed from the soviet area reached by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/long-march">Long March</a>, it was recognised as a special region by the Nationalist government under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-united-front">Second United Front</a>. There <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a> consolidated his leadership, and the party developed policies it later applied across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shaan-gan-ning-border-region.jpg" alt="Shaan-Gan-Ning Border Region" width="320" height="340" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ericmetro · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Shaan-Gan-Ning.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
